ntry>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KINOSHITA, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGITA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERASAKA, KIYOTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMIHASHI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An article coated with a fluororesin having a base material of the aticle, an elastomer layer formed thereon, and a thermally melting fluororesin layer as an outermost layer, characterized in that it is prepared by a method in which the elastomer layer is first cured at a temperature of the melting temperature of the fluororesin layer or lower until a degree of curing reaches 70 to 99.9 %, and then the thermally melting fluororesin layer is formed through the melting of the fluororesin.  The article is free from defects of a coating which conventionally occur during forming a thermally melting fluororesin coating, has a smooth thermally melting  fluororesin surface layer and is excellent in working durability of a 2-layer coating.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un article recouvert d'une fluororésine constituant le matériau de base de l'article et sur laquelle est formée une couche élastomère et une couche de fluororésine de thermofusion formant la couche la plus externe. Cet article se caractérise en ce que la couche élastomère est d'abord durcie à une température de fusion de la couche de fluororésine ou à une température inférieure jusqu'à un degré de durcissement compris entre 70 et 99,9 % ; puis la couche de fluororésine de thermofusion est obtenue par la fusion de la fluororésine. L'article est exempt de défauts de revêtement qui apparaissent généralement lors de la formation du revêtement de fluororésine de thermofusion, et il présente une couche superficielle lisse, ainsi qu'une excellente durabilité avec un revêtement double couche.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>